# Host-only artifacts that must never enter the image build context.
#
# The model-server virtualenv is created on the host by `make model-server` / `make up-gpu`; its
# `bin/python` is a symlink to a host Python that does not resolve inside the Linux builder, which
# crashes build-manifest.mjs's file walk (statSync ENOENT) and fails the app-test image build. CI
# has no host venv, so this only bit local `make build`/`make redeploy` after `make up-gpu`.
**/.venv
services/model-server/.venv
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc

# The weights: ~1.8 GB the `models` stage fetches into a BuildKit cache mount and verifies against
# models.lock.json, so they must never travel as context — which is once per image target, on every
# build. docker/Dockerfile's models stage already documents the exclusion; the line was missing.
models

# Installed by the `deps` and `prod-deps` stages from the lockfile. Sending the host's copy adds
# ~1 GB per target, and the build stage's `COPY . .` then laid the host platform's native modules
# (re2) over the ones npm ci had just built for the image.
node_modules
**/node_modules

# Rebuilt inside the image; a stale host copy would be copied over the fresh output.
build

# Runtime scratch, created on the host for the collector's bind mount by `make up`. It reached
# 225 MB of telemetry here, which was most of what remained of the context.
tmp
